        "id": 1069689013,
        "node_id": "PR_kwDOExPvac4vULE9",
        "number": 11,
        "title": "Add optional themeOptions on FocusRingScope",
        "user": {
          "login": "taingk",
          "id": 18054036,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDU0MDM2",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/taingk",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "labels": [],
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 2,
        "created_at": "2021-12-02T15:36:27Z",
        "updated_at": "2022-09-14T14:25:38Z",
        "closed_at": "2022-09-14T14:25:38Z",
        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "draft": false,
        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/focus-rings/pulls/11",
          "merged_at": "2022-09-14T14:25:38Z"
        },
        "body": "Add light and dark css var and fix brightness calculation to allow these colors. \r\nBrightness is a value from 0 to 1 and by default set to 0.2.\r\nThe prop themeOptions is optional and if undefined, Focus ring will have the same behavior as before. Otherwise, It will use light & dark theme (if saturation > 0.4).\r\nMoreover, saturation could be part of themeOptions but I chose not to touch it.\r\n\r\nExample : \r\n```\r\n<FocusRingScope containerRef={containerRef}>\r\n```\r\nNo behavior change, it will still be primary or white ring\r\n\r\n```\r\n<FocusRingScope themeOptions={{ brightnessTreshold: 0.3 }} containerRef={containerRef}>\r\n```\r\nIf the background brightness is 0.4, ring will be set to dark\r\n\r\n```\r\n<FocusRingScope themeOptions={{ brightnessTreshold: 0.3 }} containerRef={containerRef}>\r\n```\r\nIf the background brightness is 0.2, ring will be set to light\r\n\r\n\r\nIts an answer to this issue => https://github.com/discord/focus-rings/issues/8",
        "reactions": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/focus-rings/issues/11/reactions",
